+
+ private:
+  // A widget copied onto one of the exported pages may belong to a field
+  // whose name, type or value lives on a /Parent field dictionary, rather
+  // than on the widget itself (the shape LiveCycle and most authoring tools
+  // write a hierarchical field in). CPDF_PageOrganizer::UpdateReference,
+  // used to copy everything else the page reaches, treats a dictionary's
+  // "Parent" key as a structural back-edge and leaves it pointing at src()
+  // -- correctly for a page's own /Parent (the source Pages tree, handled
+  // separately below) and for an outline item's, but for a field's /Parent
+  // that leaves the copied widget naming an object in the *source*
+  // document, so it would arrive without its name or type, and a later
+  // save would write "Parent" naming an object that is not its parent in
+  // the saved file (#452). CopyFieldAncestor copies the chain explicitly
+  // instead: it returns the destination object number of `src_field` (`0`
+  // if `src_field` is null), copying it first if this is the first time it
+  // is reached. Each level's own /Kids is rebuilt to hold only the kids
+  // already copied by the time it is built -- another widget on one of the
+  // pages exported so far (found in the object number map), or a child
+  // field whose own copy (found the same way, recursively) is not empty --
+  // so a field split across an export by page keeps exactly the part that
+  // came across; a widget on a page this exporter did not copy is dropped
+  // from its parent's /Kids, the same way megapdf_page_delete drops a
+  // field left with no widgets. The chain's true root (no /Parent of its
+  // own) is registered under dest()'s /AcroForm /Fields the first time it
+  // is reached.
+  uint32_t CopyFieldAncestor(RetainPtr<const CPDF_Dictionary> src_field);
+
+  // Registers `dest_field_obj_num` under dest()'s /AcroForm /Fields, once.
+  void RegisterRootField(uint32_t dest_field_obj_num);
+
+  // After every page in `page_indices` has been copied (so every widget on
+  // them already has a destination object number), points each copied
+  // widget that names a /Parent field at the destination copy of its field
+  // ancestry (see CopyFieldAncestor). Done as a pass over the already-
+  // copied pages, rather than inline in ExportPages's per-page loop, so a
+  // field shared between two of the pages being exported is copied, and
+  // registered, only once.
+  void CopyFormFieldHierarchies(pdfium::span<const uint32_t> page_indices);
+
+  // Destination object numbers of the root fields already registered under
+  // dest()'s /AcroForm /Fields, so a field reached from two different
+  // widgets is not listed twice.
+  std::set<uint32_t> registered_root_fields_;
